---
import AsterLayout from "../../layouts/AsterLayout.astro";
import { ASTER_DEX_ID, AUTHORS, SITE_URL } from "../../entity";
import { buildAsterPageGraph, buildBreadcrumbs } from "../../lib/schema";
import { ASTER_DOCS, ASTER_ELIGIBILITY, ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED } from "../../data/aster";

const url = `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/eligibility/`;
const description =
  "Aster DEX eligibility: the restricted jurisdictions published in its terms, the 18+ requirement, and the risks of trading perpetuals with up to 1001x leverage.";

const termsUrl = `${ASTER_DOCS}resources/terms-and-conditions`;

const pageNode = {
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "@id": `${url}#webpage`,
  url,
  name: "Aster DEX eligibility and risk disclosure",
  description,
  inLanguage: "en",
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${SITE_URL}/#website` },
  dateModified: ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED,
  about: { "@id": ASTER_DEX_ID },
  author: { "@id": AUTHORS.kirsty.id },
  editor: { "@id": AUTHORS.maksim.id },
  citation: [{ "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "Aster terms and conditions", url: termsUrl }],
};

const breadcrumbs = buildBreadcrumbs(`${url}#breadcrumbs`, [
  { name: "Home", url: `${SITE_URL}/` },
  { name: "Aster DEX", url: `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/` },
  { name: "Eligibility", url },
]);

const graph = buildAsterPageGraph([pageNode, breadcrumbs]);
---

<AsterLayout
  title="Aster DEX Eligibility and Risk Disclosure | Maksim Sokal"
  description={description}
  canonical={url}
  graph={graph}
  trail={[{ label: "Eligibility" }]}
  modified={new Date(ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED)}
  ogType="website"
>
  <header class="space-y-5 max-w-3xl">
    <span class="text-xs font-mono text-amber-400 uppercase tracking-widest block">Compliance</span>
    <h1 class="font-display font-medium text-3xl md:text-4xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight leading-tight">
      Eligibility and risk
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Aster's terms restrict access by jurisdiction and require users to be at least 18. Leveraged perpetual trading
      can lose the entire deposit. This page summarises the published constraints; it is not legal advice and it is not
      a substitute for the official terms.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-400">
      Verified <time datetime={ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}>{ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}</time> against{" "}
      <a href={termsUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">the official terms</a>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="jurisdiction-heading">
    <h2 id="jurisdiction-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Restricted jurisdictions</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
      The published terms state that the services are not available to anyone who resides in, is located in, is
      incorporated in, or has a registered office in the following jurisdictions:
    </p>
    <ul class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-2">
      {ASTER_ELIGIBILITY.map((jurisdiction) => (
        <li class="bg-rose-500/5 border border-rose-400/15 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 text-xs text-rose-200/90 font-mono">
          {jurisdiction}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
      The prohibition also extends to jurisdictions subject to comprehensive sanctions and to anyone on a restricted-party
      list. The list above is a summary; the operative wording is in the official terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="age-heading">
    <h2 id="age-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Age and identity</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
      Users must be at least 18 and legally able to enter into the terms. Aster may apply identity verification and may
      suspend access where verification is not completed. Providing a false location to bypass a restriction is itself a
      breach of the terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="risk-heading">
    <h2 id="risk-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Leverage risk</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">1001x is not a free option</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          At 500x and above, margin cannot be added to an open position. A small adverse move can liquidate the
          position, and the maximum net profit ROI is capped at roughly 300% at 1001x and 500% at 500x/750x.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">Slippage and funding</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Fixed 0.01% slippage applies to BTC/USD in Degen Mode; other pairs use fixed or dynamic slippage. Funding is
          peer-to-peer, is charged periodically, and can move the liquidation price against you.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">Smart contract and peg risk</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Audits cover specific contracts at a point in time. They do not guarantee the deployed code, the oracle, the
          bridge or the stablecoin peg. USDF depends on delta-neutral backing and 1:1 redemption.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">No advice</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Nothing on this site is financial, investment, legal or tax advice. Past performance is not indicative of
          future results. If you do not understand the liquidation mechanics, do not use leverage.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-amber-500/5 border border-amber-400/20 rounded-xl p-6 space-y-2" aria-label="Scope of this page">
    <h2 class="font-display font-medium text-sm text-amber-200 tracking-wide">What this page is</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      A dated summary of the constraints published by Aster, written for readers of this independent guide. It is not
      legal advice, it does not create a relationship with Aster, and it does not authorise access from a restricted
      jurisdiction.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      See also:{" "}
      <a href="/disclosure/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">disclosure</a> ·
      <a href="/aster-dex/fees/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">fees</a> ·
      <a href="/aster-dex/contracts/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">contracts</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-[#1e293b]/60 pt-6 space-y-2">
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Written by <a href="/kirsty-moreland/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Kirsty Moreland</a> · Technical review by{" "}
      <a href="/about/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Maksim Sokal</a> ·{" "}
      <a href="/disclosure/" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-sky-300">Disclosure</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</AsterLayout>
